 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Lisse purity of the transported complex",
 "statement": "Let $C_0$ be a smooth geometrically connected affine curve, let\n$C'_0$ be a smooth geometrically connected curve containing $C_0$\nas a dense open with finite complement, let\n$g:C'_0\\to\\mathbf A^1_{k_0}$ be a finite generically etale morphism,\nlet $j:C_0\\hookrightarrow C'_0$, and let $\\mathcal F$ be lisse and\npunctually $\\iota$-pure of weight $w$ on $C_0$. Put\n$\\mathcal K:=g_*j_!\\mathcal F$ and let $B$ be the branch locus of\n$g$. Then the restriction $\\mathcal K|_W$ to\n$W:=\\mathbf A^1_{k_0}\\setminus(B\\cup g(C'_0\\setminus C_0))$\nis lisse and punctually $\\iota$-pure of weight $w$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-a1/sk-thm-dl-a1-upper/lem-a1-reduction-lisse-pure.md",
  "place": "node lem-a1-reduction-lisse-pure, order 2799"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "On the open\n$W:=\\mathbf A^1_{k_0}\\setminus(B\\cup g(C'_0\\setminus C_0))$\nthe morphism $g$ is finite etale, all of its inverse image lies\nin $C_0$, and\n$\\mathcal K|_W=g_*(j_!\\mathcal F)|_W$ sheaf-theoretically, so the\nlissity and the punctual purity of weight $w$ in the sense of\n[def-weil-punctual-weights] follow from\n[lem-a1-finite-map-purity].",
   "uses": [
    "def-weil-punctual-weights",
    "lem-a1-finite-map-purity"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
